      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"The existing `Schools::UsageController#show` action currently trusts the incoming `supply` and `period` request parameters and uses them directly, which can trigger security warnings and runtime errors. Implement robust validation so that only a predefined set of supply values (e.g., `electricity` and `gas`) and period values (e.g., `daily` and `weekly`) are accepted. When both parameters are present and valid, the action must proceed normally and return a successful HTTP response (status 200). If either parameter is missing, not required, or contains a value outside the allowed set, the action must not raise an exception; instead it should issue an HTTP redirect (status 302) to an appropriate fallback location such as the school’s main page. The controller must no longer invoke user‑controlled methods via `send` or similar dynamic calls; any logic that previously relied on `send` should be refactored to use safe, explicit method calls after validation. The implementation must satisfy the test suite, which verifies that a GET request with `supply: 'electricity'` and `period: 'daily'` receives a successful response, while a request with an invalid `supply` value (e.g., `'something'`) results in a redirect. No other external behavior should change.\"\n",
          "id": "prt_ee5a3c1f6001SER0YRyzqZmZk0",
          "sessionID": "ses_11a5c3e23ffe5OxIBycQ3QUzkG",
          "messageID": "msg_ee5a3c1f50015qTOQuLQ872AfL"
        }
